  "id": "linux-nvidia-dgx-spark-2x-qwen38-flash-next-atlas",
  "name": "2x DGX Spark Qwen3.8 Flash Next NVFP4 Atlas (SparkQwen RC16)",
  "version": 1,
  "summary": "Two directly connected Sparks running the Atlas SparkQwen RC16 engine over the private fabric, serving the unmodified nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4 checkpoint with its built-in MTP head: up to eight requests of up to 262144 tokens from one shared BF16 KV pool. Additive only: no default model, no aliases.",
  "description": "This recipe installs SparkQwen RC16 at the immutable product revision recorded in backends/atlas-sparkqwen/pins.json. LLooM owns orchestration, admission, worker-first startup, readiness, routing and telemetry. The Atlas engine image is built from Enntity/sparkqwen by that repository's install/build.sh and published to GHCR; LLooM commits no engine source. The engine (Atlas-Inf/atlas with SparkGLM's upstream series and SparkQwen's Qwen3.8-Flash-Next work on the Enntity/atlas fork) is AGPL-3.0-only and runs from its own container image. Setup acquires the pinned checkpoint, pulls the pinned image by its immutable manifest digest (the mutable tag is never pulled), and verifies the image's arm64 architecture, io.enntity.sparkqwen.install-tree contents label and in-image contract. The checkpoint is served as published: no overlay conversion and no separate drafter (speculation uses the checkpoint's own MTP head). Tools and reasoning are qualified by SparkQwen; structured output is implemented by the engine but untested with this model, and image input is not claimed.",
  "license": {
    "id": "MIT",
    "name": "Recipe metadata, launcher and orchestration"
  },
  "provenance": {
    "createdBy": "lloom",
    "generatedBy": "manual-curated",
    "source": "SparkQwen RC16: Enntity/sparkqwen 0cf2436de5211b41edf4d92071180c75cec31dd8 (install tree e7268337a5c8e77c874c7cb7be689f80a79946a5), engine Enntity/atlas sparkqwen/atlas-20261010-rc16 @ 1c43247d (AGPL-3.0-only, recorded in the image's /opt/atlas/source-manifest.json). The image is ghcr.io/enntity/atlas-sparkqwen:e7268337a5c8, addressed by its GHCR manifest digest in pins.json. The engine argument vector ships inside the image as /opt/atlas/profiles/8x262k.json, selected with SPARKQWEN_PROFILE=8x262k: eight sequences of up to 262144 tokens, BF16 KV (about 3.19M pool tokens at the profile's 0.88 GPU memory utilization), prefix caching, MTP speculation (up to 7 drafts), content-loop steering. Model nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4 revision fc694b54fb0174e0913e6adf86691ef85a4ead47."
  },
