    "testedMachine": "Two directly connected DGX Spark systems",
    "notes": [
      "Candidate lane: SparkQwen qualified RC16 on its own launcher (results/2026-10-10-rc16 in Enntity/sparkqwen); no live run through LLooM is recorded yet.",
      "TP2 with expert parallelism 2 across the private ConnectX RoCE fabric. MASTER_ADDR, FABRIC_INTERFACE and FABRIC_HCA come from the cluster node config. FABRIC_HCA and NCCL_IB_HCA are the node's explicit, node-local cluster.nodes[ID].fabricHca list (exact RDMA device names, no :port syntax); LLooM requires it on every participating node and never guesses an HCA from the NIC name, and FABRIC_SIBLINGS=0 stops the engine from adding a backchannel. Explicit lists may include both verified rails.",
      "The worker is admitted first (rank 1) and readiness-checked through its container state; the leader starts second (rank 0), serves 127.0.0.1:8893 (fixed by the image) and owns routing.",
      "Peak container memory is capped at 114 GiB per node with the profile's 4096 MiB load-time OOM guard; nothing else should use the pair's GPU memory while it serves.",
      "Licenses: the Atlas engine in the image is AGPL-3.0-only (not included in LLooM). nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4 is under the NVIDIA Open Model License per its model card; read it before use."
    ]
  },
  "requirements": {
    "platforms": ["linux-arm64"],
    "memoryGb": 114,
    "diskGb": 140,
    "commands": ["docker", "node"],
    "accelerators": ["cuda", "nvidia-gpu", "blackwell", "gb10"],
    "cluster": {
      "nodes": 2,
      "provider": "nvidia-sync",
      "topology": "direct"
    }
  },
  "backend": {
    "id": "docker-atlas-sparkqwen",
    "name": "Pinned Atlas SparkQwen image",
    "type": "openai-compatible-server"
